 "text": "If it's dark when you wake up, your body thinks it's still night. Someone asked me this, class at 7.30 up at 6.45 and no sunlight, three fixes. Your body clock sets itself by light and a room lamp is dim next to even a gray sky. Daylight at lunch is hours late. One, every light on the moment you're up. Two, get outside at the first daylight before 10 if you can. A gray sky counts. Three, same wake time every single day, that's what locks it in. Lights on outside by 10 same wake time. Send this to someone who wakes up in the dark. That's what demure is for. You archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one fix a day, this afternoon 400 words and still no coffee. If you want to try it out, I've put the link in the bio.",
